1
00:00:04,568 --> 00:00:06,403
[Nanako] Long time no see, Kasuga.

2
00:00:08,071 --> 00:00:10,782
I guess it's been...
three years now? [chuckles]

3
00:00:10,866 --> 00:00:13,118
It's so crazy bumping into you like this!

4
00:00:13,201 --> 00:00:14,369
Ah...

5
00:00:14,453 --> 00:00:15,579
Yeah.

6
00:00:16,705 --> 00:00:17,914
-Nanako?
-Yes?

7
00:00:18,415 --> 00:00:19,416
Who is this?

8
00:00:19,499 --> 00:00:22,044
Just a classmate from junior high.

9
00:00:23,629 --> 00:00:27,966
I'm on my way to a concert
with my boyfriend. Aren't we?

10
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:29,718
-[boyfriend] Yep.
-[Nanako chuckles]

11
00:00:29,801 --> 00:00:30,802
[Takao] I see...

12
00:00:30,886 --> 00:00:31,887
Ah.

13
00:00:32,387 --> 00:00:33,430
Hey, I know.

14
00:00:33,513 --> 00:00:35,599
Let's exchange contact info.

15
00:00:36,099 --> 00:00:37,476
Sure.

16
00:00:37,559 --> 00:00:38,852
[Nanako] Let me see...

17
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:43,398
There we go.

18
00:00:44,232 --> 00:00:45,734
I'll send a text just in case.

19
00:00:47,861 --> 00:00:49,071
Sent.

20
00:00:50,739 --> 00:00:52,157
[phone chimes]

21
00:00:54,034 --> 00:00:55,035
[Nanako] Good.

22
00:00:55,118 --> 00:00:56,745
CAN WE TALK? HOW'S THIS WEEKEND?

23
00:00:57,662 --> 00:00:59,122
See you around, then.

24
00:01:00,082 --> 00:01:02,084
-Let's go. [chuckles softly]
-[boyfriend] Sure.

25
00:01:06,254 --> 00:01:08,340
[♪ opening theme music playing]

26
00:02:03,979 --> 00:02:06,231
THE FLOWERS OF EVIL

27
00:02:06,314 --> 00:02:09,734
EPISODE 10

28
00:02:09,818 --> 00:02:11,236
[indistinct chatter]

29
00:02:16,950 --> 00:02:17,951
-Hi ya!
-[groans]

30
00:02:18,034 --> 00:02:19,745
-[Aya giggles]
-[breathing heavily]

31
00:02:20,871 --> 00:02:23,039
[Aya] I'm so sleepy.

32
00:02:23,623 --> 00:02:25,876
I couldn't fall asleep at all last night.

33
00:02:25,959 --> 00:02:28,253
I ended up working on the prologue.

34
00:02:29,212 --> 00:02:30,255
Nice.

35
00:02:32,924 --> 00:02:34,176
[Aya] The thing is,

36
00:02:34,259 --> 00:02:35,677
I want to ask for a favor.

37
00:02:41,141 --> 00:02:44,352
I've decided not to read other books
until I finish writing mine.

38
00:02:44,436 --> 00:02:46,646
So, I want you to hold on to this for me.

39
00:02:52,861 --> 00:02:57,032
Kasuga, did something happen between you
and that girl we met last night?

40
00:02:58,116 --> 00:03:00,160
[Takao] Not really...

41
00:03:00,243 --> 00:03:02,204
We were just in the same homeroom class.

42
00:03:02,287 --> 00:03:03,955
[bell ringing]

43
00:03:07,042 --> 00:03:09,461
Okay, then. I'll keep this safe.

44
00:03:21,139 --> 00:03:22,307
[Nanako] What's wrong with you?
STYLE
::cue()

45
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:23,391
I know.

46
00:03:23,475 --> 00:03:27,562
Did I upset your girlfriend
by suggesting we meet?

47
00:03:29,314 --> 00:03:32,067
Tokiwa and I aren't dating or anything.

48
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:33,443
You're not?

49
00:03:36,112 --> 00:03:39,991
Look, they have pizza, too!
So many choices.

50
00:03:47,332 --> 00:03:49,876
[exclaims] The food's great, isn't it?

51
00:03:51,795 --> 00:03:53,004
Saeki,

52
00:03:55,006 --> 00:03:57,551
how have you been doing... since then?

53
00:03:58,218 --> 00:04:01,346
[groans softly] I don't
remember very well.

54
00:04:01,930 --> 00:04:04,391
I was in Juvenile Detention
for about a month,

55
00:04:04,474 --> 00:04:08,019
and then we moved to Utsunomiya.

56
00:04:09,312 --> 00:04:11,064
But, really, I don't remember much.

57
00:04:11,815 --> 00:04:16,319
I've made friends in high school, though.

58
00:04:16,403 --> 00:04:18,113
I have a boyfriend now, too.

59
00:04:18,822 --> 00:04:19,864
So...

60
00:04:20,615 --> 00:04:22,576
I guess I'm happy and stuff.

61
00:04:24,369 --> 00:04:25,370
I see.

62
00:04:25,453 --> 00:04:26,454
Yeah.

63
00:04:28,290 --> 00:04:29,583
How about you, Kasuga?

64
00:04:31,293 --> 00:04:32,377
After what happened...

65
00:04:32,878 --> 00:04:34,254
How have you been doing?

66
00:04:39,968 --> 00:04:41,261
Kasuga,

67
00:04:42,971 --> 00:04:44,472
are you happy right now?

68
00:04:46,516 --> 00:04:47,976
What about Nakamura?

69
00:04:49,436 --> 00:04:50,437
After that...

70
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:53,189
How has she been doing?

71
00:04:55,025 --> 00:04:56,109
I don't know.

72
00:04:57,444 --> 00:04:58,987
I haven't seen her since.

73
00:05:01,156 --> 00:05:02,949
I don't even know where she is now.

74
00:05:06,661 --> 00:05:07,662
[Nanako] Why?

75
00:05:10,957 --> 00:05:13,376
Why don't you know
what happened to Nakamura?

76
00:05:19,925 --> 00:05:22,260
You were trying to die together, right?

77
00:05:23,470 --> 00:05:26,806
But Nakamura pushed you away.

78
00:05:27,974 --> 00:05:30,477
That's what it looked like to me.
Am I wrong?

79
00:05:31,102 --> 00:05:33,355
Why do you think she did that?

80
00:05:33,897 --> 00:05:36,191
Why did Nakamura shove you, Kasuga?

81
00:05:37,651 --> 00:05:39,069
Don't you know?

82
00:05:43,073 --> 00:05:44,157
When I saw that...

83
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:48,453
I thought, "Serves you right."

84
00:05:49,746 --> 00:05:52,374
Watching you two fail to die,

85
00:05:52,457 --> 00:05:54,459
being forced to live miserably...

86
00:05:54,542 --> 00:05:56,419
I started laughing uncontrollably.

87
00:05:57,712 --> 00:05:59,714
If you two had died that day,

88
00:06:00,298 --> 00:06:01,925
I would have been so frustrated,

89
00:06:02,008 --> 00:06:03,927
I might have lost my mind.

90
00:06:06,054 --> 00:06:07,263
I...

91
00:06:07,931 --> 00:06:09,182
I...

92
00:06:11,059 --> 00:06:12,268
Even though I did that...

93
00:06:13,353 --> 00:06:14,980
I don't feel like dying anymore.

94
00:06:19,901 --> 00:06:21,653
Tokiwa, was it?

95
00:06:23,363 --> 00:06:24,698
Do you...

96
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:26,282
like her?

97
00:06:28,994 --> 00:06:30,245
I...

98
00:06:32,122 --> 00:06:34,666
I want to read the novel she writes.

99
00:06:35,959 --> 00:06:39,629
She let me read the plot,
and it was really interesting.

100
00:06:40,338 --> 00:06:42,674
She's writing that novel now,
STYLE
::cue()

101
00:06:43,842 --> 00:06:45,844
-and I...
-Liar.

102
00:06:47,345 --> 00:06:50,473
Are you going to make her miserable, too?

103
00:06:53,268 --> 00:06:55,270
She's a replacement for Nakamura.

104
00:06:56,354 --> 00:06:58,231
A tool to make you feel better.

105
00:06:58,314 --> 00:06:59,607
You're wrong.

106
00:06:59,691 --> 00:07:01,109
[Nanako] You haven't changed at all.

107
00:07:01,192 --> 00:07:03,319
You use people any way you please,

108
00:07:03,403 --> 00:07:05,405
and throw them out
when it becomes too much.

109
00:07:05,488 --> 00:07:06,948
[Takao bangs table]

110
00:07:08,324 --> 00:07:09,784
That's not true.

111
00:07:16,916 --> 00:07:18,001
It is.

112
00:07:19,127 --> 00:07:20,420
Just watch.

113
00:07:21,796 --> 00:07:22,797
I know,

114
00:07:23,298 --> 00:07:25,550
because that girl isn't Nakamura.

115
00:07:26,634 --> 00:07:29,512
You can't face anyone other than Nakamura.

116
00:07:29,596 --> 00:07:31,765
So, you end up having to throw them out.

117
00:07:31,848 --> 00:07:33,933
[♪ tense music playing]

118
00:07:35,101 --> 00:07:36,561
Then again...

119
00:07:37,645 --> 00:07:41,274
You never actually faced Nakamura either,
did you?

120
00:07:44,402 --> 00:07:46,905
You just kept running away the whole time.

121
00:07:47,697 --> 00:07:49,866
Running away from everything.

122
00:07:51,618 --> 00:07:53,119
I knew.

123
00:07:54,037 --> 00:07:55,747
I knew that would happen.

124
00:07:57,248 --> 00:07:58,374
Still...

125
00:08:00,752 --> 00:08:02,337
I'm disappointed.

126
00:08:11,805 --> 00:08:13,848
Excuse me, I'd like to pay now.

127
00:08:15,016 --> 00:08:17,018
[Takao sobbing]

128
00:08:25,944 --> 00:08:27,737
[phone ringing]

129
00:08:35,453 --> 00:08:37,163
[line ringing]

130
00:08:40,834 --> 00:08:42,126
[flips phone shut]

131
00:08:45,755 --> 00:08:47,257
[sighs]

132
00:08:49,342 --> 00:08:50,802
[phone vibrating]

133
00:08:55,932 --> 00:08:58,643
KOJI

134
00:09:14,450 --> 00:09:16,995
[Aya] Were you busy this weekend?

135
00:09:17,537 --> 00:09:20,290
You didn't take any of my calls.

136
00:09:23,042 --> 00:09:24,711
Was it about the novel?

137
00:09:26,963 --> 00:09:28,965
[Aya] Once I started writing, I dunno...

138
00:09:29,549 --> 00:09:31,759
There wasn't much there, I guess.

139
00:09:33,469 --> 00:09:34,596
I'm disappointed.

140
00:09:35,430 --> 00:09:37,390
I didn't know my writing was this bad.

141
00:09:38,266 --> 00:09:39,601
Don't say that.

142
00:09:44,522 --> 00:09:45,732
Actually...

143
00:09:47,442 --> 00:09:51,404
Koji's been asking to make up,

144
00:09:51,905 --> 00:09:55,617
and he says
he also wants to apologize to you, Kasuga.

145
00:09:57,911 --> 00:10:01,080
But, you don't want
to see him again... right?
STYLE
::cue()

146
00:10:04,083 --> 00:10:05,418
[Koji] I'm sorry for the other day!

147
00:10:06,252 --> 00:10:07,420
I was out of line.

148
00:10:07,503 --> 00:10:10,673
Koji, please keep it down.

149
00:10:11,507 --> 00:10:13,259
[Takao] No, I'm the one who should--

150
00:10:13,343 --> 00:10:14,552
No!

151
00:10:14,636 --> 00:10:17,138
I'm really sorry
for saying those nasty things.

152
00:10:17,889 --> 00:10:19,224
To be honest, that day,

153
00:10:19,724 --> 00:10:21,726
I thought you might take Aya from me,

154
00:10:21,809 --> 00:10:23,519
and that's all I could think about.

155
00:10:24,103 --> 00:10:25,897
I'm sorry to you, too, Aya!

156
00:10:26,397 --> 00:10:27,899
-I'll change!
-Hey, Koji?

157
00:10:27,982 --> 00:10:28,983
Can you just...

158
00:10:29,901 --> 00:10:30,944
Ah...

159
00:10:33,821 --> 00:10:37,533
If anything, I feel more confident
after overcoming this crisis with you.

160
00:10:38,493 --> 00:10:41,120
Really? Did you learn your lesson?

161
00:10:41,204 --> 00:10:42,705
[Koji] I swear!

162
00:10:45,166 --> 00:10:47,710
Could you... accept my apology?

163
00:10:54,634 --> 00:10:55,718
[Koji sighs]

164
00:10:56,844 --> 00:10:58,221
I really appreciate it!

165
00:11:00,556 --> 00:11:01,808
-I'll call you!
-[Aya] See you.

166
00:11:01,891 --> 00:11:03,851
-You too, Kasuga! See you around.
-[Aya] Sure.

167
00:11:03,935 --> 00:11:05,186
Koji, over here.

168
00:11:05,270 --> 00:11:07,063
-Get back to work, please.
-[Koji] Ah.

169
00:11:13,736 --> 00:11:15,154
[Aya] Kasuga,

170
00:11:17,865 --> 00:11:19,492
you must think...

171
00:11:20,285 --> 00:11:21,828
I'm an idiot, right?

172
00:11:23,371 --> 00:11:24,372
What?

173
00:11:24,872 --> 00:11:26,249
Why would you say that?

174
00:11:29,252 --> 00:11:31,379
[Aya] No reason.

175
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:37,010
[Takao] Tokiwa!

176
00:11:41,097 --> 00:11:42,098
What is it?

177
00:11:43,474 --> 00:11:44,559
[exhales]

178
00:11:45,351 --> 00:11:46,394
Sorry.

179
00:11:47,061 --> 00:11:48,730
It's nothing. Forget it.

180
00:11:57,905 --> 00:12:00,408
DECEMBER 24TH

181
00:12:00,491 --> 00:12:03,244
[student 1] It's December 24th.
What comes to mind?

182
00:12:03,328 --> 00:12:04,495
[student 2] Santa!

183
00:12:04,579 --> 00:12:06,080
-[student 1] Snow!
-[indistinct chatter]

184
00:12:06,164 --> 00:12:07,623
[student 2] Reindeer!

185
00:12:07,707 --> 00:12:09,042
Sleighs!

186
00:12:09,125 --> 00:12:10,668
-Presents!
-[exclaims]

187
00:12:10,752 --> 00:12:12,337
[student 1] Fir tree!

188
00:12:15,465 --> 00:12:17,091
[Koji] Aya!

189
00:12:17,175 --> 00:12:18,801
[Aya] You're so loud.

190
00:12:18,885 --> 00:12:21,304
-Why did you come through the gate?
-[Koji laughing]

191
00:12:22,597 --> 00:12:25,141
-I'm tired of waiting!
-[Aya chuckles]

192
00:12:25,933 --> 00:12:28,603
[Koji] Why do you have work today,
of all days?

193
00:12:28,686 --> 00:12:30,646
-[Aya] I told you.
-[Koji chuckles]

194
00:12:42,033 --> 00:12:43,409
[electricity crackling]

195
00:12:49,207 --> 00:12:50,291
[clattering]

196
00:12:56,506 --> 00:12:59,550
[Takao's shadow]
You haven't changed a bit.

197
00:13:02,595 --> 00:13:05,390
You don't actually want
to read Tokiwa's novel.

198
00:13:06,099 --> 00:13:09,185
You just want to be the person
who got to read it.

199
00:13:12,063 --> 00:13:13,314
Isn't that right?

200
00:13:14,482 --> 00:13:15,942
That's not true.

201
00:13:16,734 --> 00:13:18,861
[Takao's shadow]
You're just like a parasite.

202
00:13:19,779 --> 00:13:21,447
It used to be on books,

203
00:13:22,031 --> 00:13:23,032
then on Saeki,

204
00:13:23,116 --> 00:13:24,367
then on Nakamura.

205
00:13:25,201 --> 00:13:26,786
And next,

206
00:13:27,286 --> 00:13:30,123
you're going to use Tokiwa and her novel
for yourself.

207
00:13:30,623 --> 00:13:31,666
You're wrong!

208
00:13:32,208 --> 00:13:35,211
[Takao's shadow] Then why did
Nakamura shove you away?

209
00:13:36,796 --> 00:13:38,214
Why do you not understand?

210
00:13:39,715 --> 00:13:42,718
It's because you didn't try
to face anybody!

211
00:13:44,262 --> 00:13:46,347
You're the one who destroyed it all.

212
00:13:47,723 --> 00:13:48,975
You destroyed Saeki,

213
00:13:49,559 --> 00:13:50,810
you destroyed your family,

214
00:13:51,561 --> 00:13:53,396
and you destroyed Nakamura, too.

215
00:13:53,479 --> 00:13:55,606
[♪ eerie music playing]

216
00:14:04,407 --> 00:14:05,575
[Takao] That's not true...

217
00:14:06,159 --> 00:14:08,703
The person Nakamura was back then is gone.

218
00:14:10,663 --> 00:14:12,039
[♪ gentle music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

219
00:14:12,123 --> 00:14:13,332
She doesn't exist

220
00:14:14,876 --> 00:14:16,377
anywhere in this world.

221
00:14:17,753 --> 00:14:19,088
It's true.

222
00:14:19,172 --> 00:14:20,423
It's all true.

223
00:14:21,716 --> 00:14:22,717
I...

224
00:14:23,217 --> 00:14:28,181
hurt and broke Nakamura and everyone else.

225
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:32,018
I might never be forgiven for what I did.

226
00:14:33,311 --> 00:14:34,729
But, still...

227
00:14:35,688 --> 00:14:39,525
Still, the person I need to be facing now,
in this moment, is...

228
00:14:43,279 --> 00:14:45,031
Kasuga,

229
00:14:49,952 --> 00:14:51,537
you must think...

230
00:14:52,163 --> 00:14:53,789
I'm an idiot, right?

231
00:14:56,792 --> 00:14:57,960
Tokiwa,

232
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:03,341
you've been suffering all alone.

233
00:15:05,134 --> 00:15:06,260
This whole time,

234
00:15:07,178 --> 00:15:08,971
you've suppressed your true self...

235
00:15:12,141 --> 00:15:13,601
[wind howling]

236
00:15:19,732 --> 00:15:21,275
I can't do that.

237
00:15:22,443 --> 00:15:26,614
I can't keep living
in the world as a ghost!

238
00:15:32,745 --> 00:15:34,038
[squelching]

239
00:15:38,834 --> 00:15:39,961
[wind stops blowing]

240
00:15:48,261 --> 00:15:49,387
[Takao inhales]

241
00:15:51,597 --> 00:15:52,682
[door opens]

242
00:15:52,765 --> 00:15:54,183
[Aya] Here you go.

243
00:15:57,687 --> 00:15:59,146
-[door opens]
-[wind chimes tinkling]

244
00:15:59,230 --> 00:16:01,607
-Welcome!
-[Koji] Welcome!

245
00:16:04,777 --> 00:16:05,987
[Takao panting]

246
00:16:07,738 --> 00:16:09,240
Tokiwa...

247
00:16:13,744 --> 00:16:14,954
I love you!

248
00:16:15,788 --> 00:16:17,623
Please go out with me!

249
00:16:22,336 --> 00:16:23,421
[laughing]

250
00:16:26,090 --> 00:16:27,091
Hey!

251
00:16:27,591 --> 00:16:31,470
What kind of joke is this?
And on Christmas Eve, of all days?

252
00:16:33,055 --> 00:16:34,932
Calm down for a minute. Have a seat.

253
00:16:35,016 --> 00:16:36,017
[Takao] Tokiwa.

254
00:16:37,852 --> 00:16:39,228
Wait a second.

255
00:16:39,979 --> 00:16:41,772
I'm on the clock right now.

256
00:16:41,856 --> 00:16:43,607
I'll be taking a break soon, so...

257
00:16:44,191 --> 00:16:45,318
Tokiwa.

258
00:16:46,986 --> 00:16:48,487
Come to me.

259
00:16:49,989 --> 00:16:51,407
I want you in my life!

260
00:16:53,117 --> 00:16:55,286
I'll kill your ghost for you.

261
00:16:56,037 --> 00:16:57,246
Let's get off

262
00:16:57,330 --> 00:16:58,873
these tracks.

263
00:17:03,502 --> 00:17:05,087
I'm in love with you!

264
00:17:07,048 --> 00:17:09,550
Seriously, what's gotten into you?

265
00:17:11,552 --> 00:17:13,679
Sorry for the commotion, everyone.

266
00:17:14,347 --> 00:17:16,182
-Hey.
-Tokiwa.

267
00:17:16,932 --> 00:17:18,601
-Tokiwa!
-[Koji] Drop it already!

268
00:17:18,684 --> 00:17:19,769
You're causing trouble!

269
00:17:20,269 --> 00:17:21,520
Koji...

270
00:17:24,774 --> 00:17:25,858
I'm sorry.

271
00:17:26,859 --> 00:17:27,860
What?

272
00:17:27,943 --> 00:17:29,570
[♪ pleasant music playing]

273
00:17:29,654 --> 00:17:30,655
What?

274
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:33,532
What do you mean by "sorry"?

275
00:17:37,912 --> 00:17:38,913
Manager...

276
00:17:39,622 --> 00:17:41,248
-What?
-[Aya] I'm sorry.

277
00:17:41,957 --> 00:17:43,501
I'll be quitting as of today.

278
00:17:43,584 --> 00:17:45,378
[manager] What the... Quit? Aya?

279
00:18:05,106 --> 00:18:06,774
-[door opens]
-[wind chimes tinkling]

280
00:18:10,528 --> 00:18:11,570
Manager...

281
00:18:13,906 --> 00:18:15,741
Do you mind if I go on break?
STYLE
::cue()

282
00:18:37,596 --> 00:18:39,098
[both panting]

283
00:18:39,181 --> 00:18:40,516
[Takao chuckling]

284
00:18:43,269 --> 00:18:44,311
[Aya chuckles]

285
00:18:47,148 --> 00:18:49,900
I forgot my bag.

286
00:18:50,818 --> 00:18:51,986
[Takao exclaims softly]

287
00:18:54,864 --> 00:18:56,157
[Aya] And this apron...

288
00:18:56,949 --> 00:18:58,909
I'll have to wash it and give it back.

289
00:19:02,496 --> 00:19:03,497
Sorry...

290
00:19:08,043 --> 00:19:09,587
[laughing]

291
00:19:23,893 --> 00:19:25,811
[♪ music continues]

292
00:19:51,837 --> 00:19:52,880
[breath trembling]

293
00:19:55,841 --> 00:19:57,051
So warm.

294
00:20:09,355 --> 00:20:10,523
[both laughing]

295
00:20:17,530 --> 00:20:20,407
FINAL CHAPTER

296
00:20:27,581 --> 00:20:28,749
Kasuga!

297
00:20:28,833 --> 00:20:31,210
[exclaims] I didn't look, I promise!

298
00:20:31,836 --> 00:20:33,879
When do I get to read it, though?

299
00:20:34,505 --> 00:20:35,756
Soon.

300
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:37,925
Just as soon as I'm done writing.

301
00:20:38,008 --> 00:20:39,635
[♪ soft music playing]

302
00:20:39,718 --> 00:20:41,178
[keyboard clacking]

303
00:20:45,641 --> 00:20:46,851
[indistinct chatter]

304
00:21:05,828 --> 00:21:07,204
[Aya] Beautiful, isn't it?

305
00:21:09,707 --> 00:21:10,749
[Takao] Yeah.
STYLE
::cue()

306
00:21:13,627 --> 00:21:15,004
Is it really okay?

307
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:18,841
Is it really okay for me to be this happy?

308
00:21:20,134 --> 00:21:21,218
[Aya] What was that?

309
00:21:22,219 --> 00:21:24,096
I'm happy too, you know?

310
00:21:31,353 --> 00:21:32,396
That reminds me.

311
00:21:32,938 --> 00:21:35,566
There's somewhere I want to go
during spring break.

312
00:21:36,692 --> 00:21:37,693
Where?

313
00:21:38,569 --> 00:21:40,821
The town you were born in.

314
00:21:41,614 --> 00:21:43,198
I want to see it.

315
00:21:45,284 --> 00:21:46,869
There's nothing to see.

316
00:21:47,369 --> 00:21:50,080
It's just a plain old, rural town.

317
00:21:53,042 --> 00:21:54,043
[phone ringing]

318
00:22:02,009 --> 00:22:03,010
Hello?

319
00:22:04,803 --> 00:22:06,513
-[door opens]
-Welcome home.

320
00:22:06,597 --> 00:22:07,765
[Shizue] Welcome home.

321
00:22:10,976 --> 00:22:13,562
Grandpa's been taken to the hospital?

322
00:22:13,646 --> 00:22:16,690
It's not looking too good.
Mom and I will go see him tomorrow.

323
00:22:18,609 --> 00:22:20,611
You can stay here, Takao.

324
00:22:23,614 --> 00:22:25,616
[indistinct chatter]

325
00:22:25,699 --> 00:22:27,451
[♪ foreboding music playing]

326
00:22:32,998 --> 00:22:34,750
[squelching]

327
00:22:46,845 --> 00:22:48,013
I'm coming with you.

328
00:22:48,514 --> 00:22:50,849
TO BE CONTINUED

329
00:22:50,933 --> 00:22:52,935
[♪ closing theme music playing]

330
00:23:47,990 --> 00:23:49,033
ON THE NEXT EPISODE

331
00:23:49,116 --> 00:23:52,745
[narrator] Kasuga is dragged back
to his past after seeing Saeki again.

332
00:23:52,828 --> 00:23:55,581
He visits his hometown
for the first time in three years.

333
00:23:55,664 --> 00:23:57,374
Next, on Episode 11,

334
00:23:58,125 --> 00:24:01,837
Kasuga finally finds a lead
that could help him find Nakamura.

335
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:02,921
Translated by Yuka Kristi

